From: Sweetspot <noreply@sweetspot>
Subject: [PATCH] Session mode: one long-lived CamillaDSP, rate changes over the websocket

The plugin forks CamillaDSP at every hw_params (every change of sample
rate or format), from the real-time thread of the player, and waits for it
to exit at hw_free. Sweetspot wants one instance per session, started by
the supervisor:

- fifo: named pipe CamillaDSP reads as its stdin (opened read/write by the
  supervisor, so it never sees EOF). The plugin opens it for writing; if
  nobody reads it, hw_params fails with ENODEV instead of forking.
- ws_port, config_rate_prefix: at hw_params the plugin asks the websocket
  server of CamillaDSP (127.0.0.1) for GetConfigFilePath and, if it is not
  <prefix><rate>.yml, sends SetConfigFilePath and Reload. CamillaDSP keeps
  its PID and reopens only its devices. It reads stdin and looks at commands
  only between two chunks, so one chunk of silence follows the reload.
- ws_timeout_ms (default 500): timeout of each websocket call; the whole
  setup in hw_params is bounded to three times that.
- The count of frames written (for the chunk boundary) restarts when the
  FIFO is a new one, i.e. when the supervisor restarted CamillaDSP.
- tail_frames, chunk_frames: at hw_free the plugin writes the tail of the
  filters as silence, up to a chunk boundary (a partial chunk would wait for
  data), closes the pipe and does not wait for the process.
- In this mode the plugin offers only S32_LE stereo.

Without "fifo" the behaviour is the original one.

Signed-off-by: Sweetspot <noreply@sweetspot>
---
